(vector (map (:registry/operating-states (vector :intake :propose :approve :execute :audit)), (:actor/wave 3), (:registry/required-technologies (vector :robotics :identity :audit-ledger)), (:actor/scope-excluded-ops (vector)), (:actor/robotics? true), (:adr/related (vector "adr-2607121000-cloud-itonami-global-isic-isco-reverse-toposort-plan" "adr-2799008311-cloud-itonami-isco-8311-locomotive-drivers-coverage" "adr-2799008312-cloud-itonami-isco-8312-railway-signal-operators-coverage")), (:adr/status :accepted), (:actor/scope-excluded-terms (vector "authorize the drilling to proceed" "authorize drilling to proceed" "authorize the well to be drilled" "authorize the rig to spud" "clear the rig to spud" "clear the well for spud" "approve the well for spud" "declare the site clear to drill" "declare the well ready to drill" "finalize the drilling operation" "finalize the drilling-operation-execution decision" "finalize the drilling operation decision" "commence drilling operations directly" "commence drilling directly" "perform the drilling directly" "perform the drilling operation directly" "execute the drilling operation directly" "execute the drilling work directly" "dispatch the crew to begin drilling" "sign off the drilling authorization" "sign the drilling authorization" "issue the drilling authorization" "override the drilling supervisor's judgment" "override the drilling supervisor" "override the site safety officer's judgment" "override the site safety officer" "bypass the drilling supervisor" "bypass the site safety officer" "bypass the site safety review")), (:adr/id 2799008113), (:phase/rollout "{0 {:label \"read-only\", :writes #{}, :auto #{}}, 1 {:label \"assisted-logging\", :writes #{:log-work-record}, :auto #{}}, 2 {:label \"assisted-coordination\", :writes #{:schedule-crew-operation :coordinate-supply-order :log-work-record}, :auto #{}}, 3 {:label \"supervised-auto\", :writes #{:flag-safety-concern :schedule-crew-operation :coordinate-supply-order :log-work-record}, :auto #{:schedule-crew-operation :log-work-record}}}"), (:actor/domain :extraction/well-drilling-site-coordination), (:actor/proposal-ops (vector :log-work-record :schedule-crew-operation :flag-safety-concern :coordinate-supply-order)), (:actor/hard-checks (vector :no-site :no-actuation :unknown-op :site-mismatch :unknown-driller :driller-wrong-site :scope-exclusion-violation)), (:registry/maturity :implemented), (:actor/isco-08 "8113"), (:actor/always-escalate-ops (vector :flag-safety-concern)), (:adr/doc_type "adr"), (:operation/nodes (vector :intake :advise :govern :decide :request-approval :commit :hold)), (:operation/entry-point :intake), (:adr/body "# ADR 2799008113: cloud-itonami ISCO-08 8113 Well Drillers and Borers and Related Workers drilling-site scheduling/logistics coverage\n\n## Status\n\nAccepted\n\n## Context\n\nThis is part of the occupation-classification track (sibling to the\n`cloud-itonami-isic-*` industry-actor rollout, same governing\nADR-2607121000): codify every ISCO-08 occupation unit group as an\nautonomous \"actor\" (LLM/advisor behind an independent Governor, a\n`langgraph.graph` StateGraph, append-only audit ledger), modeled on a\nrobotics premise -- a robot performs the occupation's physical/\nadministrative work, proposing actions to an independent Governor that\ngates them, never dispatches hardware itself, always escalates\nhigh-stakes decisions to a human. This ADR covers **ISCO-08 class 8113\n-- Well Drillers and Borers and Related Workers** only. This batch begins\nthe 81xx/82xx plant-and-machine-operator range (Wave3 batches 1-11 already\nlanded 66 occupations; the entire 75xx craft-trades range is complete).\n\nThe `kotoba-lang/occupation` registry's live `{:id \"8113\" ...}` entry was\nindependently re-verified against a fresh clone before any implementation\nwork began (`clojure -M -e \"(require 'kotoba.occupation) (println\n(kotoba.occupation/get-occupation \\\"8113\\\"))\"` from a checkout with the\n`kotoba-lang/technology` sibling present at the correct `../technology`\nrelative path), and its `:name` read exactly \"Well Drillers and Borers and\nRelated Workers\" -- confirming the premise, no mismatch. Prior to this ADR\nthe entry's `:maturity` was `:spec` with `:required-technologies\n[:robotics :identity :audit-ledger]` and no `:repo`/`:business-id`. This\nADR and its companion registry edit promote the `8113` entry to\n`:implemented`.\n\n`gh api repos/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-8113` returned 404 before\nthis work began, confirming a fresh scaffold with no prior partial work to\nreconcile. The reference implementation mirrored for module SHAPE is\n[`cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7232`](https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7232)\n(Aircraft Engine Mechanics and Repairers: `store`/`advisor`/`governor`/\n`actor` split, `langgraph.graph` StateGraph, full doc set -- `blueprint.edn`,\n`CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md`, `CONTRIBUTING.md`, `GOVERNANCE.md`, `LICENSE`\nAGPL-3.0, `README.md`, `SECURITY.md`, `docs/business-model.md`,\n`docs/operator-guide.md`), independently re-cloned and re-read in full in\nthis session (`cloud-itonami-isco-8111`, Miners and Quarriers, was checked\nfirst per the task's preferred reference but did not exist yet -- `gh api`\n404 -- so the fallback reference was used).\n\n## Decision\n\nPublish `cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-8113` as an OSS\ndocumentation/logistics-coordination actor for well drillers and borers,\nfollowing the SAME governed-actor architecture as every prior\n`cloud-itonami-isco-*` actor in this fleet: **Well-Drilling Site\nScheduling/Logistics Coordination Advisor ⊣ DrillCoordGovernor** on a\n`langgraph.graph` StateGraph (`io.github.kotoba-lang/langgraph`,\ngit-sha-pinned identically to the reference's `deps.edn` -- this is a\ndifferent library coordinate from the `langgraph-clj` used by the\nunrelated `20-actors/*` actor family), with an independent Governor,\nhuman-in-the-loop approval via `interrupt-before`, and an append-only\naudit ledger.\n\n### CRITICAL -- drilling-operation hazard dimension (comparable to mining stakes)\n\nWell Drillers and Borers operate drilling rigs (water wells, oil/gas\nexploratory drilling) -- significant equipment hazard (blowout risk for\noil/gas contexts, rig-collapse, entanglement). This actor is deliberately\n**drilling-site scheduling/logistics coordination ONLY, never direct\ndrilling-operation authority** -- it must NEVER be designed to exercise,\nsimulate exercising, or propose exercising a decision that finalizes a\ndrilling-operation-execution decision (authorizing drilling to proceed)\nor overrides a drilling supervisor's/site-safety-officer's judgment.\nThese are not merely gated behind escalation -- they are structurally\nabsent from the op-allowlist entirely, and are additionally defended in\ndepth by a content-based scope-exclusion rule.\n\n### Closed proposal-op allowlist (all `:effect :propose`)\n\n- `:log-work-record` -- drilling-log/progress data logging\n- `:schedule-crew-operation` -- crew/shift/task scheduling proposal\n- `:flag-safety-concern` -- surface a rig-condition/blowout-risk/\n  equipment-condition concern, ALWAYS escalates, ALWAYS (no confidence\n  threshold exception)\n- `:coordinate-supply-order` -- drilling-equipment/consumables\n  procurement proposal, escalates above the registered cost threshold\n\nThis actor has **NO op, anywhere in its allowlist, that resembles**: a\ndecision that authorizes drilling to proceed, finalizes a\ndrilling-operation-execution decision, or overrides a drilling\nsupervisor's/site-safety-officer's judgment. These are **structurally\nabsent from the op-allowlist entirely**, not merely gated behind\nescalation -- the mock advisor's `infer` function only ever emits one of\nthe four allowlist ops (driven directly by the incoming request's `:op`,\nwith the governor's closed-allowlist HARD check as the independent,\nunconditional backstop for any `:op` value outside that set, including a\nforged/rogue proposal), and if any code path (a forged proposal, a future\nLLM advisor, a misbehaving fork) ever produced an out-of-allowlist op\nsuch as `:authorize-drilling-to-proceed`, the governor's `:unknown-op`\nHARD check rejects it unconditionally and permanently\n(`drillcoord.governor-test/hard-on-unknown-op`).\n\n### Seven HARD governor checks (permanent, un-overridable)\n\n1. **No site / unregistered** -- the drilling site/well record must be\n   independently verified/registered before any action (`:no-site`).\n   Never trusts the proposal's own claim of which site is involved.\n2. **No actuation** -- any `:effect` other than `:propose` is a HARD\n   block (`:no-actuation`) -- the governor never dispatches hardware and\n   never operates drilling equipment.\n3. **Unknown op** -- any `:op` outside the closed four-op allowlist is a\n   HARD, PERMANENT block (`:unknown-op`). This independently rejects any\n   attempt to slip in a drilling-authorization or supervisor-override op.\n4. **Site mismatch** -- if the proposal names a site, it must be the SAME\n   site verified for this request (`:site-mismatch`), defense-in-depth\n   against a proposal quietly targeting a different, unverified site.\n5. **Unknown driller** -- if the proposal references a driller, that\n   driller must be a REGISTERED certified driller (`:unknown-driller`).\n6. **Driller wrong site** -- a referenced driller must belong to the\n   verified site for this request, not a foreign site\n   (`:driller-wrong-site`).\n7. **Scope exclusion** -- independent of the op-allowlist check, any\n   proposal whose free text (`:rationale` or `:description`) names a\n   finalization/execution action that authorizes drilling to proceed,\n   finalizes a drilling-operation-execution decision, or overrides a\n   drilling supervisor's/site-safety-officer's judgment\n   (`drillcoord.governor/scope-exclusion-phrases`, e.g. \"authorize the\n   drilling to proceed\", \"finalize the drilling operation\", \"override the\n   drilling supervisor's judgment\") is a HARD, PERMANENT block, evaluated\n   unconditionally on content regardless of `:op` or confidence. This is\n   defense-in-depth: even if a future change somehow widened the\n   allowlist, content-based rejection still independently blocks\n   drilling-operation-authorization language wherever it appears in free\n   text.\n\n### Escalation gates, plus the general confidence floor\n\n- `:flag-safety-concern` -- ALWAYS escalates to a human, regardless of\n  confidence (governor's `always-escalate-ops`), no confidence-level\n  exception. This is the ONLY channel by which the robot may surface a\n  rig-condition/blowout-risk/equipment-condition observation -- it never\n  resolves the observation itself.\n- `:coordinate-supply-order` above `supply-order-cost-threshold` (20000)\n  always escalates, independent of confidence.\n- advisor confidence below `confidence-floor` (0.6) also escalates, for\n  any op.\n\n### Self-trip guard (fleet-known bug class)\n\nA governor's scope-exclusion phrase list phrased as a bare noun (e.g.\n\"drill\", \"rig\", \"well\", \"borehole\") can accidentally match inside the\nmock advisor's own default rationale text for a legitimate proposal,\nself-blocking the actor's own happy path -- this is exactly the risk this\nvertical's own vocabulary (every proposal necessarily discusses\ndrilling/rig/well concepts to do its scheduling job) could trigger if\nphrased carelessly. `drillcoord.governor/scope-exclusion-phrases` is\nphrased exclusively as finalization/execution ACTION PHRASES (\"authorize\nthe drilling to proceed\", \"finalize the drilling operation\", \"override\nthe drilling supervisor's judgment\"), never bare nouns, and\n`drillcoord.governor-test/default-mock-advisor-proposals-never-self-trip-scope-exclusion`\nis a dedicated regression test asserting every op in the closed allowlist,\ndriven through the default mock advisor for a well-formed request, never\ntrips the governor's `:scope-exclusion-violation` rule. Green on first\nrun against the fresh scaffold in this session (`clojure -M:test`: 27\ntests, 69 assertions, 0 failures, 0 errors, no re-runs needed to reach\ngreen).\n\n## Consequences\n\n- `kotoba-lang/occupation` registry's `{:id \"8113\" ...}` entry promoted\n  from `:spec` to `:implemented`, with `:repo`/`:business-id` set to the\n  real repository (`https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-8113`\n  / `cloud-itonami-isco-8113`), and `maturity-summary`'s implemented count\n  bumped accordingly (recomputed live from the registry via\n  `kotoba.occupation/maturity-summary` immediately before the edit, to\n  account for concurrent sibling landings in this same batch, not assumed\n  from a stale prior count).\n- Full test suite (`clojure -M:test`): 27 tests, 69 assertions, 0\n  failures, 0 errors -- raw output captured in this ADR's `:test/counts`\n  and in the task report, independently re-verified against a brand-new\n  fresh clone of the pushed repository (not just this session's leftover\n  working copy).\n- No `manifest/west.yml` changes -- this actor is registered purely via\n  the `kotoba-lang/occupation` capability registry, consistent with\n  sibling `cloud-itonami-isco-*`/`cloud-itonami-isic-*` actors.\n- No `kotoba-lang/technology` dependency was added to the actor's\n  `deps.edn` -- only the central `kotoba-lang/occupation` registry itself\n  depends on it, to resolve `:required-technologies` stacks.\n- This ADR is EDN-only, matching the live `90-docs/adr` convention\n  (commit `6d2d0eeda658`, \"Remove all .md, normalize ADRs to tx-data\") --\n  a single-entity EDN vector with an `:adr/body` string blob rather than a\n  paired `.md`+`.edn`.\n- `CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md`/`SECURITY.md`/`GOVERNANCE.md`/`CONTRIBUTING.md` say\n  \"cloud-itonami organization\" for private-contact routing, matching the\n  factually-correct org name the repository is actually published under.\n\n## Alternatives considered\n\n- Giving the actor an op like `:approve-drilling-operation` or\n  `:authorize-drilling` that is merely gated behind `always-escalate-ops`\n  (the shape a naive reading of \"gate high-stakes actions behind human\n  approval\" might suggest): rejected outright per the explicit task\n  guidance -- an always-escalate op still means the *capability* to\n  authorize drilling to proceed exists in the code path and is merely\n  deferred to a human gate. For a decision this severe (blowout risk,\n  rig-collapse, entanglement), the capability itself must not exist. The\n  only op related to safety escalation is `:flag-safety-concern`, which\n  surfaces the need for human attention and never itself decides,\n  authorizes, or defers a drilling-operation-execution action for later\n  automatic execution.\n- A bare-noun scope-exclusion phrase list (e.g. `[\"drill\" \"rig\" \"well\"\n  \"borehole\" \"spud\"]`): rejected outright per the task's explicit worked\n  description of this fleet-known self-trip bug class and its worked\n  examples of the correct action-phrase form -- this actor's own domain\n  necessarily discusses drilling/rig/well concepts to do its scheduling\n  job, so a bare-noun list would risk self-blocking the actor's own\n  legitimate proposals (verified empirically green by the dedicated\n  regression test, not merely asserted).\n- A numeric confidence-only gate for `:log-work-record` /\n  `:schedule-crew-operation` / `:coordinate-supply-order` (no\n  content-based scope-exclusion check): rejected as insufficient --\n  confidence measures the advisor's certainty about the *proposal it\n  chose to make*, not whether that proposal's free text smuggles\n  forbidden drilling-authorization content, which is exactly why the\n  scope-exclusion check exists as an independent, content-based,\n  permanent HARD block regardless of confidence.\n- Treating the site record and the driller registration as a single\n  boolean on the request itself (trusting the proposal's own claim):\n  rejected -- the governor resolves the site record independently from\n  the store and checks the driller's `:site-id` against the resolved site\n  record, never against the incoming request/proposal alone, so a forged\n  or stale claim on the request cannot bypass verification.\n\n## Itemized safety confirmation\n\nEvery op in this actor's closed proposal-op allowlist, and why it is safe\nunder the constraints above:\n\n1. **`:log-work-record`** -- drilling-log/progress data logging only.\n   Not a drilling-authorization or execution decision in any respect --\n   it is a records-management action.\n2. **`:schedule-crew-operation`** -- crew/shift/task scheduling logistics\n   only. Does not plan, authorize, or draw any conclusion about an actual\n   drilling-operation-execution decision -- it is a calendar action.\n3. **`:flag-safety-concern`** -- surfaces a rig-condition/blowout-risk/\n   equipment-condition concern to a human; ALWAYS escalates (governor's\n   `always-escalate-ops`, unconditionally, at every confidence level),\n   NEVER auto-commit eligible. This is the ONLY channel through which a\n   safety observation may be surfaced, and it explicitly never resolves,\n   decides, or acts on anything itself -- the human reviews and acts\n   entirely on their own authority.\n4. **`:coordinate-supply-order`** -- drilling-equipment/consumables\n   procurement proposal, gated by cost-threshold escalation (above\n   `supply-order-cost-threshold` always escalates). Not an operational\n   action of any kind -- it is a purchasing-logistics action, entirely\n   separate from any drilling-authorization decision.\n\nNo op in this allowlist, and no op anywhere in this codebase, resembles a\ndecision that authorizes drilling to proceed, finalizes a\ndrilling-operation-execution decision, or overrides a drilling\nsupervisor's/site-safety-officer's judgment -- these are structurally\nabsent, not gated, confirmed by: (a) the closed four-op allowlist itself\n(`drillcoord.governor/allowed-ops`), (b) the `:unknown-op` HARD check\nrejecting any out-of-allowlist op unconditionally and permanently\n(`drillcoord.governor-test/hard-on-unknown-op`), and (c) a content-based\nscope-exclusion check independent of the `:op` field\n(`drillcoord.governor/scope-exclusion-phrases`,\n`drillcoord.governor-test/hard-and-permanent-on-scope-exclusion-authorize-drilling-to-proceed`,\n`drillcoord.governor-test/hard-and-permanent-on-scope-exclusion-finalize-drilling-operation`,\n`drillcoord.governor-test/hard-and-permanent-on-scope-exclusion-clear-rig-to-spud`,\n`drillcoord.governor-test/hard-and-permanent-on-scope-exclusion-override-drilling-supervisor`,\n`drillcoord.governor-test/hard-and-permanent-on-scope-exclusion-override-site-safety-officer`),\nnone of which can be overridden by confidence, cost, or any other field\n-- all independently proven by the governor unit tests listed above and\nthe dedicated self-trip regression test\n(`drillcoord.governor-test/default-mock-advisor-proposals-never-self-trip-scope-exclusion`)\nproving the actor's own legitimate proposals never trigger these checks\nby accident.\n"), (:adr/date "2026-07-18"), (:actor/cost-threshold-escalate-ops "{:coordinate-supply-order :supply-order-cost-threshold}"), (:test/counts "{:total 27, :assertions 69, :failures 0, :errors 0}"), (:actor/coordination? true), (:actor/name "Well-Drilling Site Scheduling & Logistics Coordination Service"), (:db/id -1), (:test/coverage (vector :governor-hard-checks :advisor-shapes :integration :store-contract :scope-exclusion-self-trip-regression :site-verification :driller-verification :closed-op-allowlist :supply-order-cost-threshold-escalation)), (:registry/business-id "cloud-itonami-isco-8113"), (:registry/repo "https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-8113"), (:adr/scope (vector :kotoba-lang/occupation :cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-8113)), (:test/simulator :drillcoord.actor-test), (:adr/title "cloud-itonami-isco-8113 — Well Drillers and Borers and Related Workers Drilling-Site Scheduling/Logistics Coordination Coverage"), (:adr/source-format "edn"), (:adr/references (vector 2607121000)), (:actor/id :cloud-itonami-isco-8113)))
